Description: fftools: wire `-map_inlineass` option to vf_inlineass (Phase 2)
 Phase 1 (patch 0099) shipped vf_inlineass.c + .h registered and visible
 in `ffmpeg -filters`, but with no fftools-side wiring the filter is
 dormant — the public helpers (`avfilter_inlineass_append_data`,
 `avfilter_inlineass_set_storage_size`, `avfilter_inlineass_add_attachment`,
 `avfilter_inlineass_set_fonts`) are never called.
 .
 This patch lands the wiring. Backport of Plex Transcoder 1.12.3's
 fftools/plex.c subtitle hooks, adapted to jellyfin-ffmpeg 7.1.3's
 split demuxer/scheduler/decoder/filter threading model.
 .
 New surface:
 .
   - `-map_inlineass FILE:STREAM_SPEC`. Per-file output option (matches
     Plex's signature: OPT_PERFILE | OPT_OUTPUT | OPT_EXPERT). Records
     a binding {file_idx, stream_spec, ist}. Stream specifier is
     resolved against the named input file at option-parse time
     (inputs are open by the time output options run).
 .
 New file: fftools/scaleplex_inlineass.c (+ .h). Holds the global
 binding registry and three runtime hooks invoked from fftools:
 .
   - scaleplex_inlineass_opt        — option handler (above)
   - scaleplex_inlineass_link_graph — called from configure_filtergraph
     after avfilter_graph_config succeeds. Scans the filter graph for
     filters named "inlineass", binds each to the next unbound entry
     in the registry, attaches matching font streams via
     avfilter_inlineass_add_attachment, calls set_fonts, and pushes
     the buffersink output dims via set_storage_size.
   - scaleplex_inlineass_handle_subtitle — called from transcode_subtitles
     in ffmpeg_dec.c after avcodec_decode_subtitle2 succeeds. Looks up
     the binding by AVCodecContext* and forwards the decoded subtitle
     to avfilter_inlineass_append_data.
 .
 Helper added to ffmpeg_dec.c: dec_get_avctx(Decoder *) returns the
 internal AVCodecContext. Needed because the public Decoder struct
 in ffmpeg.h does not expose dec_ctx, and scaleplex_inlineass.c needs
 it to populate (and later look up) the dec_ctx → AVFilterContext map.
 .
 Threading model — process-wide libass lock:
 .
   Plex 6.x runs the transcode loop single-threaded, so libass calls
   never race. Jellyfin 7.x splits demuxer / decoder / filter / encoder
   into separate threads connected by a bounded scheduler queue.
   Three libass entry-point classes now run on different threads:
 .
     - decoder thread:  avfilter_inlineass_append_data → process_header
                        (ass_process_codec_private, ass_alloc_style)
                        + ass_process_chunk
     - filter thread:   filter_frame → ass_render_frame
                        + overlay_ass_image (reads renderer-owned
                          memory the next render call would invalidate)
     - main thread at configure_filtergraph time:
                        scaleplex_inlineass_link_graph →
                        avfilter_inlineass_{set_storage_size,
                        add_attachment, set_fonts}
 .
   libass's contract is that ASS_Library / ASS_Renderer / ASS_Track
   must each be touched from one thread at a time. A per-filter mutex
   satisfies that on paper, but in practice libass also touches
   process-wide shared state (fontconfig, FreeType cache, font
   provider) that isn't reentrant. The prior per-filter approach
   segfaulted on the filter thread the moment ass_render_frame ran
   while ass_process_chunk on the decoder thread had just driven
   fontconfig.
 .
   This patch promotes the mutex to one file-scope
   pthread_mutex_t inlineass_lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER and
   wraps EVERY libass entry into vf_inlineass.c. Mirrors Plex 6.x's
   effective single-thread behaviour without forcing
   --disable-fontconfig or per-filter private fontconfig contexts.
   Lock contention is negligible at homelab session counts (1-3
   concurrent) because libass calls are sparse and short.
 .
 AVOption table unchanged from Phase 1. Plex's argv emits
 inlineass=...:language=...:overrides=...:outline=...:shadow=...
 beyond the 6 options vf_inlineass parses. The rewriter is responsible
 for stripping those four keys before passing the filter argv through
 — keeps the filter's AVOption table identical to Phase 1, sidesteps
 the LTO/AVFILTER_DEFINE_CLASS table-truncation mystery seen on the
 prior attempt to add stubs.
 .
 Worker rewriter cleanup after this lands: drop findSidecarSubtitle
 (~30 LOC), drop the hybrid-inlineass filter rewrite mode (~50 LOC),
 drop the HLS+seek PTS-shift bracket, drop the side-ffmpeg subtitle
 extract step (~150 LOC of subtitle_extract.go + rewriter glue),
 add a 4-line regex to strip the Plex-only filter args.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/Diagonactic/plex-new-transcoder
        (Plex Transcoder 1.12.3.4973), fftools/plex.c hooks
Forwarded: not-needed
